1
00:00:00,742 --> 00:00:02,272
(Sheldon:)Yes.
Yeah? Oh, well,

2
00:00:02,276 --> 00:00:05,476
(Sheldon:)was this guy Rick from
Computer Solutions on Colorado?

3
00:00:05,480 --> 00:00:06,450
(Sheldon:)Yes.

4
00:00:06,447 --> 00:00:07,817
(Sheldon:)Yeah, well,
he does know his stuff.

5
00:00:10,852 --> 00:00:12,682
(Leonard:)After you wrap the body
in reflective tape,

6
00:00:12,687 --> 00:00:14,857
(Leonard:)the ends get Teflon tape
so we can get a tight seal.

7
00:00:14,856 --> 00:00:16,986
Like this? Oh.
Yeah, perfect.

8
00:00:16,991 --> 00:00:18,721
(Leonard:)And it helps to have
small, delicate fingers.

9
00:00:18,726 --> 00:00:20,326
(Leonard:)So don't be discouraged
if you can't do it as fast

10
00:00:20,328 --> 00:00:21,958
as me and Howard. (chuckles)

11
00:00:23,297 --> 00:00:24,667
(Howard:)I don't know
if we have enough solder

12
00:00:24,665 --> 00:00:25,895
(Howard:)to finish
these circuit boards.

13
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:27,130
(Leonard:)We had a full spool yesterday.

14
00:00:27,130 --> 00:00:27,930
(Howard:)What can I say,

15
00:00:27,935 --> 00:00:30,535
(Howard:)I play hard,
I solder even harder.

16
00:00:32,106 --> 00:00:34,106
(Bernadette:)Sometimes he solders at home
with his shirt off.

17
00:00:34,108 --> 00:00:36,108
(Bernadette:)It's like a beer commercial.

18
00:00:36,110 --> 00:00:37,840
(blows, clicks tongue)

19
00:00:38,813 --> 00:00:40,813
(Leonard:)Well, we got to make a run
to the hardware store.

20
00:00:40,815 --> 00:00:43,115
(Penny:)How can you call yourself a
scientist and run out of solder?

21
00:00:43,117 --> 00:00:45,917
(Leonard:)Well, funny story.
So, we have plenty

22
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:47,850
(Leonard:)of the 60/40
tin-to-lead ratio solder,

23
00:00:47,855 --> 00:00:50,515
(Leonard:)but the spools look a lot
like the 63/37 tin-to...

24
00:00:50,516 --> 00:00:51,156
(Penny:)Honey, honey,

25
00:00:51,159 --> 00:00:54,559
(Penny:)honey, let me stop you.
That is-is not a funny story.

26
00:00:55,696 --> 00:00:57,426
(Howard:)You want to come with us?

27
00:00:57,432 --> 00:00:58,952
(Bernadette:)I'm kind of getting
into the groove here.

28
00:00:58,956 --> 00:00:59,576
(Penny:)Yeah, you guys run

29
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:02,420
(Penny:)to the store and let the women
handle the science for a change.

